<<<
We must take account of religio-philosophic speculations with regard to the nature of Eternal Life;
===
*We must take account of* religio-*philosophic speculations with regard to the nature of Eternal Life*;
>>>

<<<
has both religio & religiosus, but only the second admits of the -otreatment, & it gives religiosophilosophic. See also HYBRID DE- RIVATIVES.
===
has both *religio* & *religiosus*, but only the second admits of the -o-treatment, & it gives *religioso-philosophic*. See also ^^HYBRID DERIVATIVES^^.
>>>

<<<
oaf. Pl. -fs, rarely -ves; see -vE(D).
===
**oaf.** Pl. *-fs*, rarely *-ves*; see ^^-VE(D)^^.
>>>

<<<
oaken. See -EN ADJECTIVES.
===
**oaken.** See ^^-EN ADJECTIVES^^.
>>>

<<<
O & oh. Usage has changed, oh having formerly been prevalent in many contexts now requiring O, & is still by no means fixed.
===
**O & oh.** Usage has changed, *oh* having formerly been prevalent in many contexts now requiring *O*, & is still by no means fixed.
>>>

<<<
The present tendency is to restrict oh to places where it has a certain independence, & prefer O where it is proclitic or leans forward upon what follows;
===
The present tendency is to restrict *oh* to places where it has a certain independence, & prefer *O* where it is proclitic or leans forward upon what follows;
>>>

<<<
which means for practical purposes that as the sign of the ` vocative (O God our help; O mightymouthed inventor of harmonies) O is invariable,
===
which means for practical purposes that as the sign of the vocative (*O God our help; O mighty-mouthed inventor of harmonies*) *O* is invariable,
>>>

<<<
& as an exclamation the word is O when no stop immediately follows it, but before any stop oh (Oh, what a lie!; Oh! how do you know that?; O for the wings of a dove!; O who will o’er the downs with me?; O worship the King!).
===
& as an exclamation the word is *O* when no stop immediately follows it, but before any stop *oh* (*Oh, what a lie!; Oh! how do you know that?; O for the wings of a dove!; O who will o'er the downs with me?; O worship the King!*).
>>>

<<<
oasis. Pl. oases, pron. -éz.
===
**oasis.** Pl. *oases*, pron. -ēz.
>>>

<<<
oaten. See -EN ADJECTIVES.
===
**oaten.** See ^^-EN ADJECTIVES^^.
>>>

<<<
oath. Pl. pron. 6dhz; -TH & -DH.
===
**oath.** Pl. pron. ōdhz; ^^-TH^^ & ^^-DH^^.
>>>

<<<
So spelt. Pl. -os; see

obbligato. -O(E)s 3.
===
**obbligato.** So spelt. Pl. *-os*; see ^^-O(E)S^^ 3.
