<<<
obdurate, adj. The OED quotations show Shakspere, Milton, & Barham, for obdur’at, & Shelley for 6’bdirat.
===
**obdurate,** adj. The OED quotations show Shakspere, Milton, & Barham, for *obdūr'at*, & Shelley for *ŏ'bdūrat*.
>>>

<<<
The former is still sometimes heard, but is old-fashioned. See PRONUNCIATION.
===
The former is still sometimes heard, but is old-fashioned. See ^^PRONUNCIATION^^.
>>>

<<<
obedient. For yours obediently &c., see LETTER FORMS.
===
**obedient.** For *yours obediently* &c., see ^^LETTER FORMS^^.
>>>

